{"table":"nodes","ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.lean_scalar_target","record":{"id":"scalar.lean_scalar_target","kind":"declaration","label":"OAI.SKValue.scalar_value_target","status":"unverified","source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-formal-targets","locator":"GroundState/MainConclusions.lean:13–15; scalar_value_target","statement":"For every W:BrownianSpace, gamma:OrderParameter and X:R→W.Omega→R, IsMinimizer W gamma and IsDiffusion W gamma X imply ScalarValueConclusion W gamma X, whose full conjunction is Model.lean:106–118.","assumption_ids":["assumptions.value_minimizer","assumptions.value_diffusion"],"evidence_ids":[],"citation_ids":["scalar-r2-26-cite-lean-scalar-target"],"boundary":"The exact SKValue model uses a coefficient on all reals with its stated interval fields, BrownianSpace and its natural filtration. Source inspected; no kernel replay, Comparator acceptance or elaborated dependency extraction is recorded.","declaration":"OAI.SKValue.scalar_value_target"},"formal_result_assurance":{"node_id":"scalar.lean_scalar_target","recorded_status":"unverified","formal_result_eligible":false,"safety_classification":"not_kernel_checked","assurance_state":"not_kernel_checked","v2_extraction_evidence_ids":[],"current_extraction_evidence_ids":[],"scope":"Recorded classification and bound evidence only; no execution authentication or mathematical acceptance."},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.lean_scalar_target","paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"stage":"long","subgraph_ref":"sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json/support/0.3.1/2f85413164f06365ea0d825befee447650da71d54080d5dd65e78a708891c560","roles":["mapped_claim"]},{"stage":"short","subgraph_ref":"sha256:cfbe950801fd334d8fd957243fa3b1f716ef609148c5f2ff97d44f9a6443d82c/papers/short.json/support/0.3.1/77f0cf29ab577b42d8caa5b2831ebfb1ca170d4b13c1ef6897cadc8e93c2a834","roles":["recorded_prerequisite"]},{"stage":"expository","subgraph_ref":"sha256:479155de953858e60f1454491ccda2215d88a4c2780e686cdfb8422481c62d9c/papers/expository.json/support/0.3.1/9dd5536bc567fc55efaa864733bf89747cea0268a8a3865dec51ddd8e2a235dd","roles":["recorded_prerequisite"]}],"direct_passages":[{"stage":"long","passage_ref":"sha256:c4249feffa26e48c24c5690f73e0de4886e40504c8c5c0e6dcb22ec94ea334da/papers/long.md/sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json/passages/formal-scalar","anchor":"formal-scalar","mapping_ref":"sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids"}]},"aligned_passages":[{"stage":"long","passage_ref":"sha256:c4249feffa26e48c24c5690f73e0de4886e40504c8c5c0e6dcb22ec94ea334da/papers/long.md/sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json/passages/formal-scalar","anchor":"formal-scalar","mapping_ref":"sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids","text":"\n<a id=\"formal-scalar-statement\"></a>\n\n### 12.2 The separate scalar statement\n\nThe second formal statement has three clauses. Given a minimizer and an\nassociated diffusion, it establishes convergence of the finite-spin\nground-state values, a bounded martingale with a spin-valued terminal\nlimit, convergence of the gradient and the value identities. Under the\nsame hypotheses and fixed $0<T<1$, it gives eventual positivity of the\nGaussian normalizers and convergence of the finite coefficient sum.\nThese are the declarations `scalar_value_target` and\n`finite_gaussian_target`. Their caller supplies the same minimizer and\nassociated diffusion. The implementation derives compact-strip bounds\nfrom `sourceStripRegularity` and the unit curvature moment from contact\nfor those objects before applying its fixed-strip helper. Those internal\ninputs are not additional hypotheses of the exported clauses. The\nconvergence clause establishes existence of the finite-spin limit.\n\nThe index match in the Gaussian statement is exact. For\n$\\Delta=T/N$ and $t_j=j\\Delta$, the Euler path uses\n$Z_1,\\ldots,Z_N$ and produces $Y_0,\\ldots,Y_N$.\nThe source normalizer indexed from zero corresponds to manuscript\n$c_1,\\ldots,c_N$; its eventual positivity covers precisely those\nnormalizers. A separate $Z_{N+1}$ performs mean-preserving rounding:\nit enters $B_{N+1}$, not another Euler increment. Thus the finite sum is\n$\\sum_{j=0}^{N}A_jB_{j+1}$ with $A_0=0$, using exactly the displayed\nindex ranges. Total definitions at $N=0$ make no extra mathematical\nclaim about the construction for $N\\ge1$. More explicitly, the\nzero-based formal quantities `coordinate N j`, `rawCoefficient ... j`\nand `normalizer ... j` correspond to $Z_{j+1}$,\n$a(t_j,Y_j)$ and $c_{j+1}$ for $0\\le j<N$. The positivity quantifiers\nare $\\exists N_0\\,\\forall N\\ge N_0\\,\\forall j<N$, simultaneously over\nthe growing mesh, for each already fixed $T$. The extra coordinate\nwith formal index $N$ is $Z_{N+1}$. The formal martingale stops at its\nterminal random variable $U$ for all later times; $U^2=1$ almost surely,\nand the gradient converges to $U$ almost surely and in $L^2$ from below\none. The internal terminal-gradient lemma proves $UX_1=|X_1|$\nwithout requiring $X_1$ to have no atom at zero. That identity is used\ninside the implementation; it is not an extra conjunct of the endpoint. See the [scalar statement][value-type] and its\n[complete dictionary](https://github.com/wcook04/lean-exposition/blob/21b1f9e995c4276fdad02377b378f11541a3d5e9/papers/qaoa-sk/source-review/scalar-value-interface.md).\n\n","span":{"start_byte":241201,"end_byte":243764,"start_line":5199,"end_line":5240},"paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=long&passage=formal-scalar","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=long&passage=formal-scalar"}],"lenses":{"prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&view=arguments&node=scalar.lean_scalar_target&assumptions=true","consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&view=arguments&node=scalar.lean_scalar_target&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&node=scalar.lean_scalar_target&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&node=scalar.lean_scalar_target&relation=prerequisites"},"relations":[{"family":"arguments","id":"field:2b8ecc59985aeeae8a250d729284bdbef1991945e9fa2cb73cdb4fbf7f68af5f","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.lean_scalar_target","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/assumptions.value_minimizer","kind":"assumption_ids","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","derived":true,"owner_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.lean_scalar_target","source_field":"assumption_ids"},{"family":"arguments","id":"field:77a5d8c944d7284fba76d4ae0bee21ccfc059395df8edbec2601610c62e5e58d","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.lean_scalar_target","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/assumptions.value_diffusion","kind":"assumption_ids","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","derived":true,"owner_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167d